1
00:00:00,260 --> 00:00:05,360
A brown government envelope sits on a
kitchen table in Kiryas Joel, New York.

2
00:00:05,480 --> 00:00:07,040
It is late afternoon.

3
00:00:07,160 --> 00:00:10,616
Next to it, there is a stack
of school notices and a shopping list

4
00:00:10,700 --> 00:00:12,080
written in Yiddish.

5
00:00:12,320 --> 00:00:14,480
Eleven people live in this house.

6
00:00:14,800 --> 00:00:18,660
That envelope decides whether
the grocery money arrives this month.

7
00:00:18,820 --> 00:00:21,780
Now step outside onto the same street.

8
00:00:21,880 --> 00:00:24,736
A volunteer ambulance
is parked at the corner,

9
00:00:24,820 --> 00:00:26,256
staffed and ready,

10
00:00:26,340 --> 00:00:28,240
and no government funds it.

11
00:00:28,340 --> 00:00:32,580
An office that lends money at no
interest is open for business.

12
00:00:32,860 --> 00:00:36,096
A private school system
runs to its own timetable

13
00:00:36,180 --> 00:00:39,140
with nobody from the state
inside the building.

14
00:00:39,260 --> 00:00:41,516
Almost everyone who hears the question

15
00:00:41,600 --> 00:00:43,500
reaches for the same picture:

16
00:00:43,600 --> 00:00:45,736
a switch in an office somewhere.

17
00:00:45,820 --> 00:00:47,156
Someone flips it,

18
00:00:47,240 --> 00:00:49,540
the money for this community stops,

19
00:00:49,640 --> 00:00:53,060
and everything you just saw
on that street has to change.

20
00:00:53,320 --> 00:00:57,476
The number attached to this argument
is one hundred thousand dollars.

21
00:00:57,560 --> 00:00:58,536
The claim,

22
00:00:58,620 --> 00:01:02,320
repeated in the biggest documentaries
made about this community,

23
00:01:02,420 --> 00:01:05,276
is that a large Hasidic family in New York

24
00:01:05,360 --> 00:01:08,036
can receive combined public benefits

25
00:01:08,120 --> 00:01:09,536
and tax credits

26
00:01:09,620 --> 00:01:12,680
worth around one hundred
thousand dollars a year.

27
00:01:12,980 --> 00:01:16,120
Say that with the attribution
it actually deserves.

28
00:01:16,420 --> 00:01:21,260
It is a figure asserted in source
reporting and in documentary commentary.

29
00:01:21,420 --> 00:01:24,676
It is not a verified official
payment to any household,

30
00:01:24,760 --> 00:01:27,460
and no agency has published it as one.

31
00:01:27,740 --> 00:01:29,136
Now the reversal.

32
00:01:29,220 --> 00:01:33,256
You would expect a community argued
about in newspapers for decades,

33
00:01:33,340 --> 00:01:34,676
audited in public,

34
00:01:34,760 --> 00:01:36,776
named in report after report,

35
00:01:36,860 --> 00:01:39,020
to be shrinking under the scrutiny.

36
00:01:39,240 --> 00:01:40,736
It is not shrinking.

37
00:01:40,820 --> 00:01:44,316
There are roughly a hundred
thousand or more Hasidic Jews

38
00:01:44,400 --> 00:01:46,356
in the greater New York area,

39
00:01:46,440 --> 00:01:50,196
and the population nearly
doubles about every twenty years.

40
00:01:50,280 --> 00:01:54,776
Kiryas Joel is the youngest
municipality in the United States

41
00:01:54,860 --> 00:01:56,316
by median age.

42
00:01:56,400 --> 00:01:58,536
In the two thousand and ten census,

43
00:01:58,620 --> 00:02:03,340
ninety-one point five percent
of its residents spoke Yiddish at home.

44
00:02:03,780 --> 00:02:06,940
Now think about the last
time you took public money.

45
00:02:07,080 --> 00:02:08,380
Not a handout,

46
00:02:08,500 --> 00:02:09,756
a tax credit,

47
00:02:09,840 --> 00:02:12,096
something the state paid on your behalf

48
00:02:12,180 --> 00:02:15,020
that you never once
described as a benefit.

49
00:02:15,200 --> 00:02:17,816
If you have ever claimed
a federal tax credit,

50
00:02:17,900 --> 00:02:22,320
you have used the same machinery that
is sitting inside that brown envelope.

51
00:02:22,420 --> 00:02:24,976
You did not think
of yourself as a recipient.

52
00:02:25,060 --> 00:02:28,540
You thought of yourself as
a taxpayer getting something back.

53
00:02:28,700 --> 00:02:31,696
The difference between you
and the household on that street

54
00:02:31,780 --> 00:02:33,256
is not the machinery.

55
00:02:33,340 --> 00:02:36,896
The difference is how many people
the machinery is being applied to

56
00:02:36,980 --> 00:02:40,340
and whether anybody thought it was
worth writing an article about.

57
00:02:40,840 --> 00:02:43,820
So here is the question
this video answers.

58
00:02:43,920 --> 00:02:48,216
What actually happens if the government
cuts this community's benefits?

59
00:02:48,300 --> 00:02:51,497
And who exactly would
be doing the cutting?

60
00:02:51,797 --> 00:02:55,237
Now, here is where it
gets genuinely interesting.

61
00:02:55,457 --> 00:02:58,253
You are almost certainly
wrong about the answer,

62
00:02:58,337 --> 00:02:59,937
and the reason is simple.

63
00:03:00,097 --> 00:03:01,713
There is no switch.

64
00:03:01,797 --> 00:03:07,193
Means-tested public benefits in the United
States are not granted to communities.

65
00:03:07,277 --> 00:03:09,233
They are granted to households,

66
00:03:09,317 --> 00:03:10,393
one at a time,

67
00:03:10,477 --> 00:03:14,073
under program rules set
by statute and regulation

68
00:03:14,157 --> 00:03:17,073
on the basis of income and household size:

69
00:03:17,157 --> 00:03:18,477
food assistance,

70
00:03:18,717 --> 00:03:19,797
Medicaid,

71
00:03:19,897 --> 00:03:21,417
housing vouchers,

72
00:03:21,517 --> 00:03:23,297
federal tax credits.

73
00:03:23,497 --> 00:03:27,493
Read those rules, and you will not find
a provision for granting or withholding

74
00:03:27,577 --> 00:03:30,253
anything according
to a household's religion,

75
00:03:30,337 --> 00:03:32,017
because there is not one.

76
00:03:32,277 --> 00:03:36,757
No eligibility determination asks
which community you belong to,

77
00:03:36,897 --> 00:03:39,277
and a government in the United States

78
00:03:39,397 --> 00:03:42,333
cannot lawfully single
out a religious group

79
00:03:42,417 --> 00:03:46,953
for exclusion from a benefit that is
generally available to everyone else

80
00:03:47,037 --> 00:03:49,497
who meets the statutory criteria.

81
00:03:49,677 --> 00:03:51,193
So the question,

82
00:03:51,277 --> 00:03:53,013
as it is usually asked,

83
00:03:53,097 --> 00:03:55,093
has no mechanism behind it,

84
00:03:55,177 --> 00:03:56,977
not a difficult mechanism,

85
00:03:57,097 --> 00:03:58,877
no mechanism at all.

86
00:03:59,237 --> 00:04:02,053
What does exist is a different lever,

87
00:04:02,137 --> 00:04:05,117
and it is far more powerful
than the grocery money.

88
00:04:05,357 --> 00:04:07,613
It is the money attached to the schools

89
00:04:07,697 --> 00:04:11,717
and the legal standard those schools
have to meet in order to keep it.

90
00:04:11,977 --> 00:04:13,617
That lever is real.

91
00:04:13,717 --> 00:04:15,537
It has already been pulled,

92
00:04:15,637 --> 00:04:19,533
and it explains why the answer this
community has given to every funding

93
00:04:19,617 --> 00:04:22,777
threat for decades has
been the same answer:

94
00:04:22,997 --> 00:04:25,113
build the institution yourself

95
00:04:25,197 --> 00:04:27,737
so the state has nothing to switch off.

96
00:04:27,837 --> 00:04:29,093
Hold on to that

97
00:04:29,177 --> 00:04:31,817
because everything else here hangs off it.

98
00:04:31,997 --> 00:04:35,013
Once you see that the load-
bearing structure on that street is

99
00:04:35,097 --> 00:04:36,353
not the envelope,

100
00:04:36,437 --> 00:04:38,373
the question changes shape.

101
00:04:38,457 --> 00:04:41,493
It stops being what
happens if the money stops.

102
00:04:41,577 --> 00:04:44,333
It becomes what the money
was ever holding up.

103
00:04:44,417 --> 00:04:48,873
If you're enjoying this investigation and
want to uncover more stories like this,

104
00:04:48,957 --> 00:04:50,617
subscribe to the channel.

105
00:04:50,717 --> 00:04:54,177
More fascinating mysteries
and discoveries are coming your way.

106
00:04:54,537 --> 00:04:57,437
Start with how the envelope
is actually filled.

107
00:04:57,657 --> 00:05:00,937
An eligibility worker does
not assess a community.

108
00:05:01,097 --> 00:05:02,833
They assess a household,

109
00:05:02,917 --> 00:05:05,273
and they assess it against two figures:

110
00:05:05,357 --> 00:05:08,877
what comes in and how many
people it has to cover.

111
00:05:09,317 --> 00:05:14,017
That second figure is the part
the argument almost always skips.

112
00:05:14,357 --> 00:05:18,413
A house of 11 and a house
of three on the same income

113
00:05:18,497 --> 00:05:20,393
are not in the same position,

114
00:05:20,477 --> 00:05:22,937
and the rules do not pretend they are.

115
00:05:23,057 --> 00:05:24,886
They receive different amounts

116
00:05:24,970 --> 00:05:28,230
because household size is
written into the formula.

117
00:05:28,390 --> 00:05:33,506
So when a very large family appears
in a news story beside a very large total,

118
00:05:33,590 --> 00:05:35,426
you are looking at arithmetic.

119
00:05:35,510 --> 00:05:38,226
The same formula applied
to the same statute

120
00:05:38,310 --> 00:05:42,586
would produce the same result for any
household that size at that income

121
00:05:42,670 --> 00:05:44,086
anywhere in the country,

122
00:05:44,170 --> 00:05:46,130
of any religion or none.

123
00:05:46,310 --> 00:05:47,486
Which means a real cut

124
00:05:47,570 --> 00:05:50,750
has to take a different form
than the one people picture.

125
00:05:50,910 --> 00:05:53,650
It has to be a change to a program rule.

126
00:05:53,810 --> 00:05:55,166
Lower a threshold,

127
00:05:55,250 --> 00:05:56,486
tighten a test,

128
00:05:56,570 --> 00:05:57,726
cap a credit,

129
00:05:57,810 --> 00:06:00,346
change how household size is counted.

130
00:06:00,430 --> 00:06:04,346
Do any of that and it applies
to every household in the program,

131
00:06:04,430 --> 00:06:07,510
because the statute has no
way of telling them apart.

132
00:06:07,670 --> 00:06:10,646
A household of two in a town
you have never visited.

133
00:06:10,730 --> 00:06:13,610
A household of 11 in Kiryas Joel.

134
00:06:14,270 --> 00:06:17,190
The rule reaches both
or it reaches neither.

135
00:06:17,390 --> 00:06:20,266
So there is no policy
that cuts this community

136
00:06:20,350 --> 00:06:22,746
and leaves everybody else where they were.

137
00:06:22,830 --> 00:06:27,726
There is only policy that cuts everybody
and happens to reach these houses harder,

138
00:06:27,810 --> 00:06:32,286
because families of 10 or more children
are common here and household size

139
00:06:32,370 --> 00:06:34,170
sits inside the formula.

140
00:06:34,470 --> 00:06:37,450
Which brings us back
to the hundred thousand dollars.

141
00:06:37,550 --> 00:06:41,846
Reporting on this community's economics
has drawn on the Yafed report covering

142
00:06:41,930 --> 00:06:44,686
2018 to 2022,

143
00:06:44,770 --> 00:06:46,886
on United States census figures,

144
00:06:46,970 --> 00:06:49,330
and on reporting in The New York Times.

145
00:06:49,530 --> 00:06:51,146
That is where the figure lives,

146
00:06:51,230 --> 00:06:54,810
and it is worth being exact
about what kind of figure it is.

147
00:06:54,910 --> 00:06:56,866
It is a combined total

148
00:06:56,950 --> 00:06:59,186
assembled across several programs

149
00:06:59,270 --> 00:07:02,106
describing what a large
household could receive

150
00:07:02,190 --> 00:07:04,750
rather than a check anybody was handed.

151
00:07:04,910 --> 00:07:08,666
How that total is put together
is a whole subject of its own,

152
00:07:08,750 --> 00:07:10,830
and this is not the video for it.

153
00:07:10,930 --> 00:07:13,710
What matters right here is only this:

154
00:07:13,910 --> 00:07:17,686
every component of it is
a household-level determination,

155
00:07:17,770 --> 00:07:20,590
and not one of them is
addressed to a community.

156
00:07:20,870 --> 00:07:24,690
And the household is not sitting
still waiting for the post.

157
00:07:24,970 --> 00:07:28,230
Women are the community's
primary paid workforce.

158
00:07:28,390 --> 00:07:32,966
That single sentence overturns most of
what gets assumed about this arrangement.

159
00:07:33,050 --> 00:07:36,786
The wages arriving in these houses
arrive largely through mothers,

160
00:07:36,870 --> 00:07:39,626
and family businesses
carry much of the rest.

161
00:07:39,710 --> 00:07:42,766
So a home on that street
usually has income.

162
00:07:42,850 --> 00:07:44,761
The argument rarely counts.

163
00:07:44,845 --> 00:07:46,281
Alongside support,

164
00:07:46,365 --> 00:07:48,661
the argument tends to count twice.

165
00:07:48,745 --> 00:07:50,861
If the envelope stopped coming tomorrow,

166
00:07:50,945 --> 00:07:53,321
it would not be stopping into a vacuum.

167
00:07:53,405 --> 00:07:55,401
It would be stopping into a house

168
00:07:55,485 --> 00:07:57,661
that already has earners in it,

169
00:07:57,745 --> 00:08:00,241
on a street that already runs services

170
00:08:00,325 --> 00:08:03,281
the state does not pay for. Now,

171
00:08:03,365 --> 00:08:06,565
here is the part that
actually decides this question.

172
00:08:06,905 --> 00:08:10,301
New York state law requires
that non-public schools

173
00:08:10,385 --> 00:08:13,181
provide instruction
substantially equivalent

174
00:08:13,265 --> 00:08:16,485
to the instruction given
in local public schools.

175
00:08:16,665 --> 00:08:18,285
That is the standard.

176
00:08:18,445 --> 00:08:21,941
It is not a funding rule
dressed up as an education rule.

177
00:08:22,025 --> 00:08:25,301
It is an education rule
with funding attached to it,

178
00:08:25,385 --> 00:08:27,661
and attached is the word that matters

179
00:08:27,745 --> 00:08:32,005
because that attachment is the only
place a genuine lever exists.

180
00:08:32,185 --> 00:08:35,141
State and city reviews of Hasidic yeshivas

181
00:08:35,225 --> 00:08:39,325
found that some of them did not meet
the substantial equivalency standard.

182
00:08:39,505 --> 00:08:42,001
Boys in strict Hasidic yeshivas

183
00:08:42,085 --> 00:08:47,061
typically study from about seven-thirty
in the morning until nine-thirty at night,

184
00:08:47,145 --> 00:08:48,981
ten or more hours a day,

185
00:08:49,065 --> 00:08:51,241
with little secular education.

186
00:08:51,325 --> 00:08:54,501
Those two sentences
are the entire dispute,

187
00:08:54,585 --> 00:08:57,741
and the argument over how that
standard should be enforced

188
00:08:57,825 --> 00:09:00,301
and over the public
funding connected to it

189
00:09:00,385 --> 00:09:02,025
has run for years.

190
00:09:02,625 --> 00:09:05,421
And notice where that
lever actually touches.

191
00:09:05,505 --> 00:09:07,681
It does not touch the grocery money.

192
00:09:07,765 --> 00:09:09,565
It touches the classroom.

193
00:09:09,685 --> 00:09:12,961
Funding attached to a school
is withheld from the school,

194
00:09:13,045 --> 00:09:15,981
which means the pressure
travels through a child's desk

195
00:09:16,065 --> 00:09:18,185
rather than through a family's kitchen.

196
00:09:18,425 --> 00:09:23,381
That is the whole reason this is the live
fight and the benefits argument is not.

197
00:09:23,465 --> 00:09:27,761
One of them has a mechanism written
into law with a named standard,

198
00:09:27,845 --> 00:09:30,821
a review process,
and a remedy at the end of it.

199
00:09:30,905 --> 00:09:33,501
The other has a number in a newspaper

200
00:09:33,585 --> 00:09:35,145
and nothing behind it.

201
00:09:35,265 --> 00:09:37,721
So what happened when
the lever was pulled?

202
00:09:37,805 --> 00:09:40,065
Not what the switch theory predicts.

203
00:09:40,165 --> 00:09:41,921
The reviews were carried out.

204
00:09:42,005 --> 00:09:43,581
The findings landed.

205
00:09:43,665 --> 00:09:48,701
The argument went into years of hearings,
objections, revisions, and litigation,

206
00:09:48,785 --> 00:09:50,645
and it is not settled now.

207
00:09:50,785 --> 00:09:52,581
Nobody has finally ruled,

208
00:09:52,665 --> 00:09:54,981
and nobody has quietly complied.

209
00:09:55,065 --> 00:09:58,005
What the community did
instead was organize.

210
00:09:58,165 --> 00:09:59,981
It turned out in numbers.

211
00:10:00,065 --> 00:10:02,081
It argued the case in public.

212
00:10:02,165 --> 00:10:03,681
It retained lawyers,

213
00:10:03,765 --> 00:10:06,601
and it kept the school
day exactly as it was

214
00:10:06,685 --> 00:10:09,017
while the argument continued around it.

215
00:10:09,177 --> 00:10:12,337
That response tells you
something the figures never will.

216
00:10:12,557 --> 00:10:16,313
Pressure applied to the money
produced a defense of the institution,

217
00:10:16,397 --> 00:10:18,217
not a modification of it.

218
00:10:18,617 --> 00:10:20,393
Look again at that street

219
00:10:20,477 --> 00:10:23,417
because this is what
the switch theory cannot see.

220
00:10:23,677 --> 00:10:25,773
The community runs Hatzalah,

221
00:10:25,857 --> 00:10:28,017
a volunteer ambulance service.

222
00:10:28,157 --> 00:10:30,937
It runs Shomrim and Shmira patrols.

223
00:10:31,097 --> 00:10:33,573
It runs Haverim for roadside help.

224
00:10:33,657 --> 00:10:35,153
It runs a beth din,

225
00:10:35,237 --> 00:10:36,573
a religious court.

226
00:10:36,657 --> 00:10:38,993
Not one of those is a state service.

227
00:10:39,077 --> 00:10:42,833
The Hebrew Free Loan Society
lends money at no interest.

228
00:10:42,917 --> 00:10:45,313
Charity funds cover specific needs,

229
00:10:45,397 --> 00:10:47,653
among them Bonei Olam,

230
00:10:47,737 --> 00:10:49,817
which funds fertility treatment.

231
00:10:49,957 --> 00:10:52,513
This community operates its own schools,

232
00:10:52,597 --> 00:10:53,713
its own courts,

233
00:10:53,797 --> 00:10:58,597
and its own emergency services instead
of relying on the public equivalents.

234
00:10:58,697 --> 00:10:59,837
Add that up.

235
00:10:59,937 --> 00:11:02,852
It is a parallel provision
of precisely the services

236
00:11:02,936 --> 00:11:05,337
a government cut would normally threaten:

237
00:11:05,477 --> 00:11:07,633
ambulances, courts,

238
00:11:07,717 --> 00:11:08,673
loans,

239
00:11:08,757 --> 00:11:09,673
schools.

240
00:11:09,757 --> 00:11:13,753
The things most exposed
to a funding decision are, here,

241
00:11:13,837 --> 00:11:15,817
the things furthest from one,

242
00:11:16,097 --> 00:11:19,513
which gives us the honest answer
to the question in the title,

243
00:11:19,597 --> 00:11:21,657
and it is not a comfortable one.

244
00:11:21,877 --> 00:11:24,893
If public support to these
households were reduced,

245
00:11:24,977 --> 00:11:28,317
the first thing to absorb
it would not be Hatzalah.

246
00:11:28,457 --> 00:11:30,377
It would not be the beth din.

247
00:11:30,497 --> 00:11:32,437
It would not be the school day.

248
00:11:32,677 --> 00:11:34,553
Those get defended first,

249
00:11:34,637 --> 00:11:38,117
and the record of the last
few decades says so plainly.

250
00:11:38,217 --> 00:11:41,297
The absorption would
happen inside the houses.

251
00:11:41,457 --> 00:11:44,873
It would land on the mothers
already carrying the paid work,

252
00:11:44,957 --> 00:11:46,597
who would carry more of it.

253
00:11:46,717 --> 00:11:48,313
It would land on the children

254
00:11:48,397 --> 00:11:49,813
in a home of eleven,

255
00:11:49,897 --> 00:11:53,353
where a reduction per person
looks small on a spreadsheet

256
00:11:53,437 --> 00:11:55,737
and looks very different on a table.

257
00:11:56,017 --> 00:12:00,037
That is the part both sides
of this argument walk past.

258
00:12:00,537 --> 00:12:03,117
The institutions are the strong points.

259
00:12:03,257 --> 00:12:05,337
The people are the soft ones.

260
00:12:05,497 --> 00:12:09,037
A cut aimed at a system
is absorbed by a family,

261
00:12:09,297 --> 00:12:12,777
and that order of priority
is the real finding here.

262
00:12:13,057 --> 00:12:14,493
Decades of pressure

263
00:12:14,577 --> 00:12:16,617
and the pattern never varies.

264
00:12:16,717 --> 00:12:18,513
Income is negotiable.

265
00:12:18,597 --> 00:12:20,473
Institutions are not.

266
00:12:20,557 --> 00:12:25,293
A community that will accept being poorer
will not accept a different school day,

267
00:12:25,377 --> 00:12:29,453
and it has said so in every forum
where the question has been put to it.

268
00:12:29,537 --> 00:12:33,486
Whether you find that admirable
or indefensible depends entirely

269
00:12:33,570 --> 00:12:37,866
on what you believe a childhood is
for, and that is a real disagreement

270
00:12:37,950 --> 00:12:39,826
rather than a misunderstanding.

271
00:12:39,910 --> 00:12:41,630
But it is not a mystery.

272
00:12:41,770 --> 00:12:43,650
It is a stated preference,

273
00:12:43,790 --> 00:12:45,646
acted on consistently,

274
00:12:45,730 --> 00:12:46,706
in public,

275
00:12:46,790 --> 00:12:49,630
for as long as anyone
has been keeping count.

276
00:12:50,050 --> 00:12:53,606
The reason a cut does not produce
the collapse people expect

277
00:12:53,690 --> 00:12:58,050
is that the thing they expected
to break was never carrying the weight.

278
00:12:58,270 --> 00:12:59,666
Now the steel man,

279
00:12:59,750 --> 00:13:02,026
and it deserves to be put properly.

280
00:13:02,110 --> 00:13:05,686
Critics, including taxpayers
and public officials,

281
00:13:05,770 --> 00:13:06,926
argue that public money

282
00:13:07,010 --> 00:13:11,306
should not support a system that leaves
children without a secular education.

283
00:13:11,390 --> 00:13:13,286
That is not a bigoted position,

284
00:13:13,370 --> 00:13:15,906
and it should not be
answered as though it were.

285
00:13:15,990 --> 00:13:20,470
It rests on a claim about children
rather than a complaint about adults.

286
00:13:20,630 --> 00:13:22,610
The argument runs like this.

287
00:13:22,750 --> 00:13:24,745
A benefit paid to a household is

288
00:13:24,829 --> 00:13:28,910
paid because a society decided
children should not go without.

289
00:13:29,390 --> 00:13:33,746
If that same society also requires that
children be taught to read and reason

290
00:13:33,830 --> 00:13:38,246
in the language of the country they
live in, then funding one obligation

291
00:13:38,330 --> 00:13:40,086
while the other goes unmet

292
00:13:40,170 --> 00:13:42,326
is not respect for a community.

293
00:13:42,410 --> 00:13:46,010
It is the abandonment
of a child in the name of respect.

294
00:13:46,250 --> 00:13:50,206
The people making that case say
the education standard exists

295
00:13:50,290 --> 00:13:53,826
to protect the children rather
than to punish the community,

296
00:13:53,910 --> 00:13:56,046
and on the plain text of the standard,

297
00:13:56,130 --> 00:13:57,270
they are right.

298
00:13:57,470 --> 00:14:00,130
That is the strongest version of the case,

299
00:14:00,250 --> 00:14:05,146
and it does not get weaker because the
community is unpopular in some quarters

300
00:14:05,230 --> 00:14:07,090
and sympathetic in others.

301
00:14:07,530 --> 00:14:09,186
Then there is a second group,

302
00:14:09,270 --> 00:14:12,030
and they are harder
to answer than the officials.

303
00:14:12,530 --> 00:14:16,146
Critics who grew up inside
these communities and left

304
00:14:16,230 --> 00:14:19,686
say the education they
received made leaving harder,

305
00:14:19,770 --> 00:14:21,090
not impossible,

306
00:14:21,190 --> 00:14:22,050
harder.

307
00:14:22,230 --> 00:14:25,206
Yiddish is the daily
language of these communities,

308
00:14:25,290 --> 00:14:28,830
and English is for many
boys a second language,

309
00:14:28,930 --> 00:14:31,670
learned late and learned incompletely.

310
00:14:31,790 --> 00:14:34,266
They describe losing not only a religion,

311
00:14:34,350 --> 00:14:35,546
but a language,

312
00:14:35,630 --> 00:14:36,706
a neighborhood,

313
00:14:36,790 --> 00:14:39,506
and an entire set of shared references.

314
00:14:39,590 --> 00:14:41,826
When they say the schooling was the wall,

315
00:14:41,910 --> 00:14:45,186
they are not speculating about
somebody else's childhood.

316
00:14:45,270 --> 00:14:47,126
They are describing their own.

317
00:14:47,210 --> 00:14:49,726
And notice what that does to the argument.

318
00:14:49,810 --> 00:14:54,086
The education question stops being
only about a taxpayer's money.

319
00:14:54,170 --> 00:14:58,844
It becomes a question about whether the
way out of a community is a door at all

320
00:14:58,928 --> 00:15:01,428
or a wall with a handle painted on it.

321
00:15:01,648 --> 00:15:03,424
So concede what is true.

322
00:15:03,508 --> 00:15:05,044
The standard is lawful.

323
00:15:05,128 --> 00:15:06,868
The findings were real.

324
00:15:07,028 --> 00:15:10,744
The concern about the children is
the serious version of this argument,

325
00:15:10,828 --> 00:15:14,148
and it has not been answered
by pointing at ambulances.

326
00:15:14,328 --> 00:15:17,244
What the community's own
conduct has established

327
00:15:17,328 --> 00:15:22,667
is narrower than its defenders sometimes
claim and narrower than its critics fear.

328
00:15:22,848 --> 00:15:26,284
It has established that money
is not the pressure point.

329
00:15:26,368 --> 00:15:28,448
That is all it has established.

330
00:15:28,568 --> 00:15:31,484
It has not made
the education question go away,

331
00:15:31,568 --> 00:15:34,584
and it has not shown that
the children in those classrooms

332
00:15:34,668 --> 00:15:37,408
are getting what a different
standard would give them.

333
00:15:37,608 --> 00:15:40,464
And yet, turn the question around

334
00:15:40,548 --> 00:15:42,828
because it was never really about them.

335
00:15:42,948 --> 00:15:45,428
Public money runs through your life too.

336
00:15:45,568 --> 00:15:50,244
It is inside the tax credit you claimed
without ever calling it a benefit.

337
00:15:50,328 --> 00:15:51,564
It paid for the classroom

338
00:15:51,648 --> 00:15:54,927
where somebody taught you to read
the words you are reading now.

339
00:15:55,067 --> 00:15:57,424
So imagine a proposal to reduce it

340
00:15:57,508 --> 00:16:00,404
and imagine being told
the reduction was conditional

341
00:16:00,488 --> 00:16:02,948
on changing how your children are raised.

342
00:16:03,088 --> 00:16:04,828
What would you give up first?

343
00:16:05,008 --> 00:16:09,244
Most people answer that question exactly
the way this community answers it,

344
00:16:09,328 --> 00:16:12,088
and they answer it
without noticing they have.

345
00:16:12,288 --> 00:16:14,244
You would take the smaller check.

346
00:16:14,328 --> 00:16:16,688
You would not take
the different childhood.

347
00:16:16,988 --> 00:16:20,404
The brown envelope on that
kitchen table in Kiryas Joel

348
00:16:20,488 --> 00:16:22,744
is not what holds that street together,

349
00:16:22,828 --> 00:16:25,444
and cutting it would not expose a secret.

350
00:16:25,528 --> 00:16:28,524
It would only confirm what
the people living there already know

351
00:16:28,608 --> 00:16:30,364
about their own priorities.

352
00:16:30,448 --> 00:16:34,904
The more useful question is what
a similar envelope and a similar threat

353
00:16:34,988 --> 00:16:36,597
would reveal about yours

